    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "**Considering Synthesis Providers**\n\nI've decided to move forward with Google Cloud Text-to-Speech. It seems the best fit, as it readily handles SSML and the desired voice/prosody controls. Now, the next step is to explore its API specifics and begin planning the Python script structure.\n\n\n**Developing the Python Script**\n\nI'm now diving into the specifics of coding `synthesize_ssml.py`. The plan is to import the Text-to-Speech client, create a function to handle SSML synthesis, and integrate provider-specific elements like the client class and model configuration. I'm focusing on the `google-cloud-texttospeech` library to get started on this. I'll get the initial file created.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789860555983,
          "start": 1789860553385
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc00a2a9001w0EQtkSZtPRt1y",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc009ea30016ivaHBjQ60sCCJ",
      "session_id": "ses_f43ff616effevx23V9a6lax347",
      "time_created": 1789860553385,
      "time_updated": 1789860555983
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "UqlguljkmQkVo9Re",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import os\nfrom google.cloud import texttospepeech\n\ndef synthesize_ssml(text, output_filename=\"output.mp3\"):\n    \"\"\"Synthesizes SSML with voice and prosody controls using Google Cloud Text-to-Speech.\"\"\"\n\n    client = texttospeech.TextToSpeechClient()\n\n    # Set the SSML input with voice and prosody controls\n    ssml_text = f\"\"\"\n        <speak>\n            <prosody rate=\"medium\" pitch=\"medium\">\n                {text}\n            </prosody>\n        </speak>\n    \"\"\"\n\n    synthesis_input = texttospeech.SynthesisInput(ssml=ssml_text)\n\n    # Configure the voice (e.g., US English, WaveNet voice)\n    voice = texttospeech.VoiceSelectionParams(\n        language_code=\"en-US\",\n        name=\"en-US-Wavenet-D\",  # Example WaveNet voice\n    )\n\n    # Select the audio file type\n    audio_config = texttospeech.AudioConfig(\n        audio_encoding=texttospeech.AudioEncoding.MP3\n    )\n\n    # Perform the text-to-speech request\n    response = client.synthesize_speech(\n        input=synthesis_input, voice=voice, audio_config=audio_config\n    )\n\n    # Write the response audio content to a file\n    with open(output_filename, \"wb\") as out:\n        out.write(response.audio_content)\n        print(f'Audio content written to file \"{output_filename}\"')\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # Example usage:\n    # Ensure you have authenticated with Google Cloud (e.g., by setting GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS)\n    # For more information, see: https://cloud.google.com/docs/authentication/getting-started\n    \n    # Simple text to demonstrate prosody control\n    synthesize_ssml(\"Hello, this is a test with a slightly slower pace and a normal pitch.\")\n",
            "filePath": "synthesize_ssml.py"
          },
